        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0654f052-be59-59a9-846a-0dab411cbc2d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Albert V of Austria; Albert the Magnanimous; Albert II of Germany\n- Organizations: Schottenkirche, Vienna; Melk Abbey; German-speaking Benedictine monks\n- Events: Melker Reform; Council of Constance\n- Roles: King of Hungary; King of Croatia\n\nFacts:\n- In 1418, Duke Albert V of Austria transferred Schottenkirche, Vienna, to German-speaking Benedictine monks from Melk Abbey during the Melker Reform.\n- The Melker Reform was initiated after the Council of Constance.\n- Albert the Magnanimous, also known as Albert II of Germany, lived from 10 August 1397 to 27 October 1439.\n- Albert the Magnanimous was King of Hungary and Croatia from 1437 until his death in 1439.",
